+| `--prefill-decode-arms, --no-prefill-decode-arms` | run the server with two arms -- a prefill context + thread and a decode context + thread that share<br/>one KV -- so a reply generating while a prompt is being processed does not wait for the prefill's steps.<br/>Refused for a speculator, mmproj/TTS/realtime,<br/>embeddings/rerank/decision, LoRA adapters, --sleep-idle, backend sampling and -np 1.<br/>This form is EXPLICIT: the server refuses to start if the pair cannot be honoured.  See<br/>--prefill-decode-arms-mode for the auto form, in which both -ib and LLAMA_SERVER_PREFILL_DUTY are<br/>deprecated (they exist to bound a decoder's stall inside a SHARED step, and on this path the decoder has<br/>its own context and thread).<br/>On a HOST-EXPERT tier (-ncmoe/-cmoe with an expert arena) the decode context's graph reserve arrives<br/>AFTER the movable-boundary slab is created, so the server declares it up front the same way an embedded<br/>MTP head's draft context is declared (a flat 3584 MiB second-context reserve, no KV term -- the pair<br/>shares one cache).  That is automatic and needs no operator input: measured clean at 1 GPU and at 3<br/>GPUs in both layer and tensor split with a default (auto) arena.  MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_AUX_RESERVE_MIB<br/>overrides the size if a shape wants a different one; a manually set GGML_CUDA_SLAB_RESERVE_MIB still<br/>wins over both, because it is the explicit operator request.<br/>(env: LLAMA_ARG_PREFILL_DECODE_ARMS) |
+| `--prefill-decode-arms-mode MODE` | 'off', 'on' or 'auto' (default: 'off').  This is an OPT-IN delivery feature: a run that does not ask<br/>for the pair allocates, reserves and logs exactly what the single-context server does.  'auto' enables<br/>the pair when the shape can carry it -- at least 2 slots, and nothing the pair refuses -- and then<br/>FALLS BACK to single-context with a warning if the decode context cannot be created; 'on' refuses to start<br/>instead, so an operator who asked for it is never silently downgraded.  An explicit --prefill-decode-arms<br/>or --no-prefill-decode-arms overrides this (whichever comes last wins).<br/>(env: LLAMA_ARG_PREFILL_DECODE_ARMS_MODE) |
